Discussion Problem: The Vessel
Take the curve
\[
x = r(y) = \sin\!\left(\frac{\pi y}{4}\right) + 1.5, \qquad 0 \le y \le 8,
\]
and spin it around the \(y\)-axis. The result is the 8 in. tall, vase-shaped vessel shown below:

// Fine sampling of the wall profile r(y), used only to draw the outline.
vesselOutlineData = {
  const yVals = d3.range(0, 8.001, 0.02);
  return yVals.map((y) =&gt; ({ y, r: r(y) }));
}







Plot.plot({
  width: 260,
  height: 420,
  x: { domain: [-3, 3], axis: null },
  y: { domain: [0, 8], label: "height (in)" },
  marks: [
    Plot.line(vesselOutlineData, { x: (d) =&gt; d.r, y: "y", stroke: "var(--bs-body-color)" }),
    Plot.line(vesselOutlineData, { x: (d) =&gt; -d.r, y: "y", stroke: "var(--bs-body-color)" }),
    Plot.ruleY([0])
  ]
})








Figure 1: The empty vessel, formed by rotating x = r(y) around the y-axis.




Suppose that the vessel starts out empty. Water is poured in at a constant rate (measured in in\(^3\)/sec), chosen so that it takes 20 seconds to completely fill the vessel.

Create Two Graphs
Based on the shape of the vessel and the provided information:

Sketch a graph of the depth of the water in the vessel versus time as it is filled up.
Similarly, sketch a graph showing how fast the depth is increasing versus time.



Compare & Collaborate
Once you have sketched both graphs, compare your work with others at your table.

Discuss any differences that you see.
Compare your reasoning and decide as a group which graph you believe is best for both.
Draw these graphs on the board.



Check Your Work
Once your answer is up on the board, use the interactive visualization below to reveal the solution.

In what ways does your group’s graph differ?
Can you explain any differences? Was there a flaw in your reasoning? Did you have the right idea and your graph just lacked precision?







